{
  "area": "mexico-riviera-maya",
  "method": "Ocean sites from Isla Mujeres and Cancún south through Puerto Morelos, Playa del Carmen, Puerto Aventuras, Akumal and Tulum's reef; Cozumel, cenotes and snorkel-only whale-shark trips are out. Official lists: CONANP's 2016 management programme for Parque Nacional Costa Occidental de Isla Mujeres, Punta Cancún y Punta Nizuc (reef units, the C-55/C-58 wrecks, MUSA galleries and the zoning that closes some units or limits them to snorkelling) and CONANP's 2000 programme for Parque Nacional Arrecife de Puerto Morelos (Regla 73 reef units); each counts once. The Mexican Caribbean tourism board's Cancún, Isla Mujeres and Puerto Morelos diving pages (read through the Wayback Machine because the live pages now redirect to generic city pages) count together as one list. Operator lists: Pocna, Mundaca Divers, Squalo Adventures, Cancún Scuba Center (its Google My Maps layer, which gives the positions used here), Solo Buceo, Aquaworld, Scuba Total, Wet Set, Koox, Pro Dive International (Playa del Carmen and Puerto Aventuras pages), Dressel Divers, Scuba Playa, Tank-Ha, Deep Mexico, Akumal Dive Shop and Akumal Dive Center; each operator counts once however many of its pages were read. A site counts when named, scuba-divable and on two independent lists; sites the park programmes close (preservation or recovery subzones) or limit to snorkelling are excluded even when an operator names them. Not counted: DivePlannerPro's generated 'reachable sites' pages, Taste of Isla's reprint of Sea Hawk's tours, the unnamed 'Isla Mujeres Trips' storefront, PADI Travel listings and blogs; Phocea Mexico's domain served a defacement page; Scuba Cancún, Mexidivers and Yucatek Divers name no ocean sites, so Tulum's reef has no named site on any counted list. Manchones 1/2 and Grande/Chico are kept as one row because no source maps one pair onto the other. Counted 2026-10-14.",
